34,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have a shortage of phenotyping technicians, though the glasshouse crew remains strong. However, our senior modelling analysts are currently seconded abroad until next autumn.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found that while the ministry still subsidizes glasshouse space, shipping costs have risen. Interestingly, simulation and modelling hours are now free, but animal-unit day rates have increased sharply.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks last year because of a lapsed contract, but the animal facility is fully accredited and has a resident vet now!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings are rather sobering; field sites are plagued by environmental disasters, and projects relying on live breeding colonies are significantly more prone to schedule overruns than computational ones.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I have discovered that catalogue-style awards tend to provide long-term value to the community, whereas mechanism-focused projects often remain unresolved. Additionally, the national repository's turnaround time has improved significantly.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate balance, is it not? We have the physical space and the glasshouse staff, but we lack the specialized technicians to analyze the results.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"It is also concerning that the cost of animal research has spiked, even as the computing side has become more accessible. We must consider how this affects the actual feasibility of the budgets.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"Wait, if the spectroscopy suite was down for so long, any project that needs it might be in big trouble! We should definitely keep that in mind.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Kenji. When we combine that with the instability of field sites and the volatility of breeding colonies, the risk profile for certain types of biological research becomes quite precarious.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"The data suggests that we should prioritize projects with a tangible, long-term output over those chasing elusive mechanisms, especially given the current instability of field and lab environments.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Servas,,"I agree with Toshio. In times of uncertainty, a project that builds a lasting resource for others is a wise investment of our limited funds.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree. If we can find a proposal that creates a lasting resource without relying on the most expensive or unstable infrastructure, that would be the most sustainable choice.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"That makes sense! So we should look for something that doesn't need the broken spectroscopy machines or the flooded field sites, right?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. We should favor projects where the primary risks are computational or based in stable environments, rather than those dependent on the whims of nature or failing hardware.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,It seems we are in alignment. We should seek a proposal that balances long-term utility with a low risk of systemic failure.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Servas,,I believe we have established a sound set of criteria. Let us now see which of the candidates best fits this profile of stability and enduring value.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. I am ready to review the candidates with these financial and operational constraints in mind.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready too! Let's see who the candidates are and find the best one!,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I concur. Let us move to the final stage and apply our findings to the specific proposals.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,pass,Toshio,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
